@startuml 08_states_dossier
!include ../style.iuml
title State machine diagram: life cycle of a dossier in the queue
hide empty description

[*] --> triaged : intake writes the dossier directly in this state\n(the event log records received -> triaged)

state "Active dossier" as Active {
  state triaged
  state explained
  state explanation_skipped
  state ready
  state leased
  state awaiting_countersign

  triaged --> ready : green lane (no finding)
  triaged --> explained : explanation kept by the guard
  triaged --> explanation_skipped : AI unavailable, guard refusal,\nbudget spent or deadline passed
  explained --> ready
  explanation_skipped --> ready
  ready --> leased : deal (lease placed)
  leased --> ready : lease expired or handed back,\nor sign-off disagreement (escalation)
  leased --> awaiting_countersign : first signature\n(high severity)
  awaiting_countersign --> leased : lease to another senior
}

leased --> decided : every finding resolved
Active --> dead_lettered : failure after the retries\n(back-off between attempts)
dead_lettered --> triaged : replayed by the administrator (level 4)\n(once only)
decided --> [*]

note right of decided
  A decided dossier is never changed. A corrected claim
  submitted again is a NEW document (version n+1) that
  starts at "triaged"; the old version stays "decided".
end note

note bottom of ready
  Every transition is one event added to the log; a
  transition from the wrong state is refused.
end note

note as N1
  <b>Defined in the code's transition table but never used:</b>
  "received" (only the origin of the first logged event) and
  "rechecked" (decided -> rechecked -> triaged). No code path
  moves a dossier into "rechecked" today.
end note
@enduml
